00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.540
Maya 300's memory bandwidth rises two and a half times, so inference stops waiting on compute. This is AI Chips &amp; Data Centres, episode 22. Microsoft has announced Azure Maya 300, and production deployments are set for 2027. Starting that same year, Microsoft says it will scale the Maya family to multi-gigawatt deployments, and make Maya the primary inference system for its products and services. Storage Review reports the part as a TSMC N2P compute die,

00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:36.260
with 8 HBM 4 stacks. Those stacks are 288 gigabytes at 18 terabytes per second.

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:45.900
The thermal design power is 950 watts. A Maya 300 rack holds 96 of those accelerators inside a 167 kilowatt envelope.

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:55.920
Each chip also has 32 ports of 400 gigabit links. Maya 200 was a monolithic N3P die with 6 HBM 3E stacks,

00:00:56.680 --> 00:01:02.760
266 gigabytes and 7.1 terabytes per second. Maya 300 splits that into a main

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:08.880
compute die, two IO dies and four memory dies. Peak compute is 13.8 peta

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:17.580
ops at FP4 and 6.9 peta ops at FP8, up from 10.1 and 5.1. That is about a 37%

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:24.340
gain in FP4 compute, 33% more memory capacity and about twice the HBM band with per

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:30.740
watt. Microsoft claims 40% more tokens per megawatt than leading GPU-based systems, and

00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:36.760
up to seven times the rack-scale token throughput of Maya 200. Maya 200 is already in production,

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:42.480
including on co-pilot. GitHub co-pilot and Microsoft Foundry are slated to follow by the end

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:49.900
of the year. Maya 300 is still a 2027 production plan, not a shipped rack. Changshin Memory Technologies

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:56.040
plans a server DDR5 RDIM on a 4F-squared DRAM cell by the end of 2026.

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:01.540
President Kau Kanyu said that at a Shanghai industry conference on October 10th,

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:04.100
Global Times and the South China Morning Post report.

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:08.000
Each cell takes four times the square of the minimum feature size,

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:11.020
against six for the mainstream 6F-squared cell.

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:17.360
Trend force, citing mydrivers, says that cut can lift density 30-50% in the same area.

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:22.840
The transistor is a vertical-surrounded gate, meant to hold the channel harder and leak less.

00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:31.900
Technode reports more than 300 patent families on the architecture, and work on hybrid bonding so the array and the peripheral logic can be built apart.

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:35.600
That is a launch plan, not a module in volume shipment.

